[0.017, "o", "\u001b[4;57r\u001b[57;1H\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;62r\u001b[47;245H┃\r\r\n \u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[1mTask complete \u001b[227C\u001b[m┃\r\r\n   └ Fixed both reported gaps on the Heineken demo (PR #71, branch \u001b[37m demo/heineken-3 \u001b[m):\u001b[158C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n\u001b[6C1. \u001b[1mStale background\u001b[m: \u001b[37m styles/backgrounds/big.svg \u001b[m had a leftover base-brand (Frescopa) raster texture overlaying the correct Heineken green fill. Stripped it. Committed (\u001b[37m aeff994 \u001b[m), pushed, deployed, verified live.\u001b[24C┃\r\r\n\u001b[6C2. \u001b[1mMissing icon\u001b[m: Root cause was an AEM content-pipeline quirk — the \u001b[37m :name: \u001b[m → \u001b[37m <span class=\"icon icon-name\"> \u001b[m server-side shortcode conversion fails when the identifier has a bare numeric segment between hyphens (e.g.\u001b[20C┃\r\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[37m heineken-3-icon \u001b[m). Verified this precisely via isolated test-page A/B experiments against the live content pipeline. Fixed by renaming the icon assets to remove the digit segment (\u001b[37m heineken-icon.svg \u001b[m, \u001b[37m heineken-beans.svg \u001b[m), updating CSS  ┃\r\r\n\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[5Creferences, and re-authoring the nav/footer/welcome content docs to use the corrected shortcodes. Committed (\u001b[37m 102d702 \u001b[m), pushed, republished, and confirmed the published pages now render actual icon spans instead of literal text.\u001b[10C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n\u001b[5CBoth fixes are live. CI (\u001b[37m deploy \u001b[m, \u001b[37m test \u001b[m) passing on PR #71. Preview: \u001b[4;36m\u001b]8;id=md-11ievwh;https://demo-heineken-3.dev.frescopamedia.com/companies/heineken-3/en/\u0007https://demo-heineken-3.dev.frescopamedia.com/companies/heineken-3/en/\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 — cleaned up all temporary /tmp scratch files.\u001b[51C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C\u001b[37m┃\u001b[m\u001b[60;3H"]
