[0.000, "o", "ix is live on the demo domain.\u001b[166C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n \u001b[33m$\u001b[m \u001b[1mShell \u001b[mVerify updated category-tiles CSS rule live on demo domain 10 lines…\u001b[164C5s ┃\r\r\n   set -o pipefail; { set -o pipefail; { sleep 5; curl -s \"\u001b[4;36m\u001b]8;id=md-mxr0tz;https://demo-heineken-3.dev.frescopamedia.com/styles/styles.css\u0007https://demo-heineken-3.dev.frescopamedia.com/styles/styles.css\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\" | grep -n -A3 \"main .section.category-tiles {\" | head -10 ; } 2>&1 | SCOUT_COMPRESS_SESSION='8bd5fbe5-b482-4899-950d-8… ┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n \u001b[34m●\u001b[m Confirmed — the conflicting \u001b[37m background: rgb(212 175 55 / 8%) \u001b[m gold tint is gone from the live deployed CSS. The landing hero should now correctly show the pale Heineken-green \u001b[37m #f1f8f1 \u001b[m background instead of the cream/gold tint.\u001b[13C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n \u001b[33m$\u001b[m \u001b[1mShell \u001b[mClean up temp files 2 lines…\u001b[207C┃\r\r\n   rm -f /tmp/commit_msg_bg2.txt /tmp/check1.svg /tmp/check_page.html 2>/dev/null; echo done\u001b[152C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n \u001b[34m●\u001b[m Found and fixed the"]
[0.000, "o", " actual root cause this time — apologies for the earlier incomplete diagnosis.\u001b[144C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n   \u001b[1mReal bug\u001b[m: \u001b[37m search-hero \u001b[m and \u001b[37m category-tiles \u001b[m are two style classes applied to the \u001b[1msame single section element\u001b[m (not stacked sections). \u001b[37m .category-tiles \u001b[m had its own full \u001b[37m background: rgb(212 175 55 / 8%) \u001b[m (a warm gold tint) declared \u001b[3mafter\u001b[m    ┃\r\r\n   \u001b[37m .search-hero \u001b[m's rule in the stylesheet. Since both selectors have equal CSS specificity, the later rule wins — and \u001b[37m background \u001b[m shorthand fully replaces all prior layers rather than merging. So \u001b[37m .search-hero \u001b[m's intended \u001b[37m --light-color \u001b[m +   ┃\r\r\n   \u001b[37m big.svg \u001b[m background was being \u001b[1mcompletely overridden\u001b[m by that gold tint on every page load. That's the \"cream\" you kept seeing — my earlier SVG raster fix was correct but was never actually rendered because of this override.\u001b[18C┃\r\r\n\u001b[244C┃\r\r\n   \u001b[1mFix\u001b[m: removed the conflicting \u001b[37m bac"]
